  "worked_solution": "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,t=q$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $q.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
